# One directory per run: `pilot1/`, and never a run written to this level.
# `run.py` refuses an --out that already holds a manifest.json.
#
# `words.jsonl` is one row per (cell, word) and runs ~80 MB per run -- 290 items
# x 8 pairs x ~100 moved words. Derived data at a size git should not carry.
#
# **BUT "REGENERATE IT" IS ONLY TRUE WHILE THE STORE HOLDS STILL.** An earlier
# version of this comment said nothing depends on the committed copy, which
# assumed re-running reproduces the file. It does not: the population is
# DISCOVERED by intersecting roster.endpoints() with the models present in
# twp_words_v4, so once an ingest lands, the same command against the same code
# writes a different population. `pilot1`'s word-level rows exist in the working
# tree and nowhere else, and that is a real exposure, not a tidy exclusion.
#
# `cells.jsonl` (~2 MB), `skipped.jsonl` and `manifest.json` ARE committed.
# `skipped.jsonl` is the record of what was NOT measured and why, and
# `manifest.json` enumerates the pairs, so together they pin a population that
# a later run cannot be compared to by name alone.
words.jsonl
